    "decision": "Individually review both complete originals and all3 hunks of the stepper interaction fix. selectedIndex now marks the old step interacted only if the index changes; bounds validation and invalid/pending/editable selection guards remain. Two old interaction tests deliberately use previous instead of next at the last step, and the added subscription test verifies assigning the same index emits no second interaction before unsubscribing. All90 old cases remain,88 complete callbacks retain semantics. The exact setter body is present in both published minimums and shipped JS after the finite signal-read/write mapping, with a transparent getter and exact zero initial state plus compiler debugName metadata. Stepper is not an owned legacy family or dependency in any of the1028 source members. Keep the public peer, no fork or modern API mirror, and retain all historical HTML/CSS/SCSS and callbacks. Source applicability only; no actual peer/runtime/floor execution. Exact compiler/Node/RxJS/peer floors, consumer/SSR/browser gates and independent audit remain separate. No publication.",
    "source_conclusion_only": true,
